    "progress": "Write-order fix: start.ts now ends the SUPERSEDED previous session BEFORE the ticket write (was after) -- the ticket write is now the sole point-of-no-return, matching stop.ts's already-safe ordering. Proven via an event-cursor-order regression test (session.takeover must precede ticket.updated). Detect+repair: new src/sessions/repair.ts (findOrphanedActiveSessions + buildHealedSession) plus listSessionsTolerant in repo/sessions.ts; wired into slop reindex (always scans, reports in the summary) and slop reindex --heal (closes out orphans: ended_at + synthesized end_summary + session.ended/orphan_repair event). Scan is skipped with a warning when the ticket read itself had problems, to avoid false positives. Filed ticket_01KYAW7DSFYVNM7NP12J9CYJDZ for the residual gap this doesn't eliminate (new-session creation must precede the ticket write that references it -- structural, needs a journal/2PC to close outright, judged out of scope here per the write-order+repair-path scope). docs/cli-reference.md updated for --heal. Full suite: 1769/1769 pass; typecheck/lint/format clean."
